    },
    "message": "Add the Rust skeleton: lane module scan, core modules and parity fuzz\n\nbuild.rs turns each src/state/*.rs and src/rules/*.rs into a module and a\nPython submodule, reached with native.rules(name) and native.state(name),\nso a lane edits neither lib.rs nor native.py.\n\ncore/mathx.rs holds CPython's float results: libm exp, expm1 and pow behind\nblack_box (LLVM rewrites pow(x, 2.0) to x * x, which gives other bits),\nhypot, sum, fsum, max, min and round. core/rng.rs has the CounterRNG draws\nand the one key builder, core/value.rs the JSON value V, core/interner.rs\nthe singletons. psychology.rs and contacts.rs now use them; a value where\nmath.exp raises is left to Python instead of being computed.\n\nclippy.toml bans the f64 methods outside mathx, and swap_remove.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
