      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jphacks/tkb_2615/git/trees/8834edaabb5110ececff57c68c861709a7064d8a"
    },
    "message": "Port sum's use of C long, which is 32 bits on Windows\n\nCPython's fast paths read ints with PyLong_AsLongAndOverflow, so on Windows an int outside\n32 bits ends them and the rest is plain addition without compensation. The parity fuzz\ncaught this on the Windows job.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
